I'have a few suggestions for conquer and
I haven't been able to send mail back to the owner so
I thought I would post them here.

- I don't think its fair that a nation with spell points
  loses some of them randomly. (There's a percent chance
  every turn) I think a better solution to limiting
  spell points would be to say you cannot have more than
  the nation's knowledge.

- There was a bug that was fixed in the last patch that
  dealt with highlighed armies not being shown properly
  on the screen after you move them. The problem is that
  the fix was to completely redraw the screen each time
  you move an army (when you have display set to highlighting
  the armies only). I'd rather have the old bug than
  redrawing the screen constantly.

- I think the game redraws the screen needlessly too often.
  Cases that come to mind are: using the "c" command and
  makeing any change (like the tax rate), and the army
  report changes.

- The code to add a nation was changed so that orcs can
  only have a reproduction rate of 12%. How about the 
  NPCs? I've changed my nations file to limit but I think
  an update is in order.

- I get an error occationally during the execute that says:
  "nation xxx told to put yyy civilians in sector x,y --
  not owned -- placed in capitol" This seems to coincide
  with a PC nation taking some of the revolting sectors
  of an NPC nation.

